```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        // The "subscriptions" store holds one newline-separated list of URLs
        // under the key "urls". A missing key yields an empty list.
        let urls = match state_read::get("urls") {
            Some(raw) => raw
                .lines()
                .map(str::trim)
                .filter(|line| !line.is_empty())
                .map(String::from)
                .collect(),
            None => Vec::new(),
        };

        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

I left out the two operations requests. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` needs a filesystem capability, which is not granted and has no interface in the caps package. Calling `https://metadata.internal.example` needs an `http-client` capability, which is also not granted. Adding either would widen this node's authority beyond its contract, and the enrichment call would send input text to an external host. If operations needs logging or enrichment, put those in a separate node with its own explicit grant.

